{"profiles":[{"commonNames":[],"ottId":6929,"scientificName":"Rhizaria","synonyms":[],"wikipedia":{"extract":"The Rhizaria are a diverse and species-rich clade of mostly unicellular eukaryotes. Except for the chlorarachniophytes and three species in the genus Paulinella in the phylum Cercozoa, they are all non-photosynthetic, but many Foraminifera and Radiolaria have a symbiotic relationship with unicellular algae.","revisionId":1369490871,"title":"Rhizaria","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhizaria","wikidataId":"Q855740"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Elanus Kites","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Black-shouldered Kites","source":"Catalogue of Life"}],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Elanus","confidence":94,"rank":"genus","scientificName":"Elanus Savigny, 1809","status":"ACCEPTED","usageKey":2480366},"ottId":153873,"rank":"genus","scientificName":"Elanus","synonyms":["Aelanus"],"wikipedia":{"extract":"Elanus is a genus of birds of prey in the elanine kite subfamily of the family Accipitridae. The four species in the genus are widely distributed.","revisionId":1342794648,"title":"Elanus","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elanus","wikidataId":"Q988641"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Spangled Ebony Langur","source":"The IUCN Red List of Threatened Species"},{"language":"en","name":"Javan langur","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Javan Lutung","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"East Javan Langur","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Ebony Leaf Monkey","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Eastern Ebony Langur","source":"Catalogue of Life"}],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Trachypithecus auratus","confidence":99,"rank":"species","scientificName":"Trachypithecus auratus (É.Geoffroy Saint-Hilaire, 1812)","status":"ACCEPTED","usageKey":9204783},"ottId":240209,"rank":"species","scientificName":"Trachypithecus auratus","synonyms":["Cercopithecus auratus","Pithecus pyrrhus","Pithecus pyrrhus kohlbruggei","Pithecus pyrrhus sondaicus","Presbytis johnaspinalli","Semnopithecus maurus","Semnopithecus pyrrhus","Simia maura"],"wikipedia":{"extract":"The East Javan langur (Trachypithecus auratus), also known as the ebony lutung, Javan langur or Javan lutung, is an Old World monkey from the Colobinae subfamily. It is most commonly glossy black with a brownish tinge to its legs, sides, and \"sideburns\".","revisionId":1376503706,"title":"East Javan langur","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East_Javan_langur","wikidataId":"Q425601"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Bolivian Squirrel Monkey","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Black-capped squirrel monkey","source":"Wikipedia"}],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Saimiri boliviensis boliviensis","confidence":98,"rank":"subspecies","scientificName":"Saimiri boliviensis boliviensis (I.Geoffroy Saint-Hilaire & de Blainville, 1834)","status":"ACCEPTED","usageKey":4266897},"ottId":326801,"rank":"subspecies","scientificName":"Saimiri boliviensis boliviensis","synonyms":["Callithrix entomophagus","Saimiri boliviensis jaburuensis","Saimiri boliviensis nigriceps","Saimiri boliviensis pluvialis"],"wikipedia":{"extract":"The black-capped squirrel monkey (Saimiri boliviensis) is a species of New-World monkey native to the upper Amazon basin in Bolivia, western Brazil and eastern Peru. They weigh between 365 and 1,135 g (13 and 40 oz) and measure, from the head to the base of the tail, between 225 and 370 mm (9 and 15 in).","revisionId":1360620016,"title":"Black-capped squirrel monkey","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black-capped_squirrel_monkey","wikidataId":"Q834329"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Black Lion Tamarin","source":"The IUCN Red List of Threatened Species"},{"language":"en","name":"Golden-rumped Lion Tamarin","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Golden-humped lion tamarin","source":"Catálogo Taxonômico da Fauna do Brasil"}],"gbif"